# Exercise: Current Working Directory
#
# `os.current-dir` returns the directory the process was launched
# from. Like `os.getenv` and `os.home-dir`, it returns *two*
# values — the path and a Bool that says whether the lookup
# succeeded:
#
# Stack effect: ( -- path status )
#
# Most of the time the lookup works, but it can fail (for example
# if the current directory was deleted out from under the process)
# so the flag is part of the contract.
#
# There is no `chdir` — the working directory is set once when
# the process starts.
#
# Your task: write `cwd-or` — return the current directory when
# available, or the given fallback string when not.
#
# Stack hint: after `os.current-dir` your stack is
# ( fallback path status ). Use the same `nip` / `drop` shape as
# in exercise 01.
#
# When done, delete the marker line below.

# I AM NOT DONE

: cwd-or ( String -- String )
    # Your code here
    drop ""
;

: test-cwd-non-empty ( -- )
    "/tmp" cwd-or string.length 0 i.>

    # Do not edit below this line
    test.assert
;
